<title>THAILAND: Thai bourse halts Union Bank shares.</title>
<headline>Thai bourse halts Union Bank shares.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Thailand on Friday halted trading in the shares of the Union Bank of Bangkok Plc.</p>
<p>The bourse said it was awaiting a material information disclosure from the bank, but did not specify what the information was.  </p>
<p>The bank's shareholders in January settled a seven-year dispute over who should control the bank.</p>
<p>The Bank of Thailand bought a 6.25 percent stake in the bank following a capital increase announced at the start of the year.</p>
<p>Union Bank of Bangkok Plc is among the smallest of Thailand's 12 commercial banks in asset terms.</p>
</text>
